{
  "text": "On this day, September 14th: In 2022: Death of Queen Elizabeth II: The Queen's coffin is taken from Buckingham Palace, placed on a gun carriage of The King's Troop Royal Horse Artillery and moved in a procession to Westminster Hall for her lying in state over the next four days with the queue of mourners stretching for miles along the River Thames. In 2000: Microsoft releases Windows Me. And in 2015: The first observation of gravitational waves is made, announced by the LIGO and Virgo collaborations on 11 February 2016.",
